<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY'S GABONA RT TO ISSUE HUF 250 MLN BONDS.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY'S GABONA RT TO ISSUE HUF 250 MLN BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian grains trading company Gabona Rt will launch 2,500 bonds with a 100,000 forints nominal value each for public domestic subscription, lead manager Buda-Cash Brokerhaz Rt said on Tuesday in the official bourse gazette.</p>
<p>    Bond name:		    Gabona Rt I</p>
<p>    Issuer:			 Gabona Rt</p>
<p>    Total amount of issue:    250 million Hungarian forints</p>
<p>    Denomination of bond:     100,000 Hungarian forints</p>
<p>    Issue price:		  nominal value</p>
<p>    Buying method:		on-the-spot cash payment</p>
<p>    Offering period:	    January 8, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date:		January 8, 2000</p>
<p>    Interest rate:		18 percent plus semiannual</p>
<p>					premium</p>
<p>    Interest payment dates:   first date 8 July 1997, and</p>
<p>					semiannually thereafter</p>
<p>    Redemption:		   To be redeemed in a lump sum on</p>
<p>					January 8, 2000</p>
<p>Note: the interest rate premium conditions are set by Gabona Rt and available upon request.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
